PLACEHOLDER -- not a certificate.

This file is embedded into the firmware so the device can pin the development
CA when OTA_SERVER_URL uses https://. Generate the real one with:

    python tools/make_dev_certs.py --ip <your-server-lan-ip>

which writes server/certs/ and overwrites this file with the CA certificate.

The build succeeds with this placeholder in place; only HTTPS connections fail,
and they fail closed. Certificate verification is never disabled to work around
a missing certificate. Plain-HTTP development URLs do not use this file at all.

A CA *certificate* is public, so committing a generated one leaks nothing. The
CA *private key* stays in server/certs/, which is git-ignored.
